# Build context exclusions. Without this file `COPY . .` ships the entire git
# history, the docs site, the screenshot and any local virtualenv into the image.

# ── Version control & CI ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.git
.gitignore
.github
.dockerignore

# ── Documentation site (not needed at runtime) ───────────────────────────────
docs
node_modules
package.json
package-lock.json
screenshot.png
README.md
QUICK-WINS.md
CHANGELOG.md
LICENSE

# ── Local development ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
venv
.venv
.env
Makefile
requirements-dev.txt
ruff.toml
tests
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache

# ── Runtime output (bind-mounted, never baked in) ────────────────────────────
reports

# ── Private configuration ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# config.yaml holds the domain list. Baking it into a published image would
# distribute it with every pull, so it is mounted at run time instead — both
# docker-compose.yml and `make docker-run` already do exactly that.
config.yaml
